# Fleet votes and their callbacks. House style: content/STYLE.md.

card dec_signal
type decision
cat mystery
clue
days 11 18
weight 10
once
duration 2
roles A B
lean curious open log
text The high-gain antenna logs a weak carrier on a frequency the fleet stopped using years ago, coming and going every 11 seconds: some retired probe's beacon, probably. {A} wants to turn a dish and answer it. {B} points out that turning the dish costs propellant the fleet hasn't got to spare.
option open | Answer it | {A} spends the propellant, and the whole fleet listens to static for an hour. Then the carrier changes pitch.
  set signal_answered
  mark t_signal
  res fuel -3
  trait A curious 5
option log | Log it, keep going | The signal goes into the anomaly log under "later". {A} tapes a printout of the waveform above their bunk, just in case.
  set signal_ignored
  mark t_signal
  morale A -5

# Weeks later: the callback for whichever way the fleet voted.
card signal_reply
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 41
roles A
when flag signal_answered
when since t_signal >= 14
text At 03:12 the dish locks onto a reply: a burst of housekeeping telemetry in a format nobody has used in years, answering a hail it shouldn't have been able to hear. {A} is the first one awake. Mission Control's reply comes 40 minutes later, in full: "say again??"
do set signal_contact
do trait A curious 4

card signal_echo
type event
cat mystery
due
once
days 25 41
roles A
when flag signal_ignored
when since t_signal >= 14
text {A} finds the carrier in the dish logs again. It's stronger now, and its bearing has drifted toward the arrival corridor. Nobody uses the word "following". The anomaly report uses the word "persistent".
do set echo_heard
do morale A -3

# Injury and rescue: needs supplies from another ship.
card crisis_eva
type event
cat grim
once
days 10 34
weight 6
roles A
when cond A ok
when kit_elsewhere A
text A micrometeoroid hits the hull during {A}'s EVA, close enough to feel through the boots. {A} secures every tool, works back along the tether hand over hand, and comes inside with a wrist that won't bend.
do cond A injured
do morale A -10
do open rescue_kit

card rescue_kit
type rescue
cat grim
duration 1
roles A B
default volunteer
when cond A injured
when bestbond B A
text {A} needs a medical kit from another ship, and the next transfer window is tight.
option send | Send the kit | A kit crosses on the next transfer. {A}'s wrist is splinted by lunch, and the anomaly report runs to four pages.
  kit A
  morale A 6
option volunteer | {B} brings it over | {B} doesn't wait for the paperwork, makes the crossing in the next window, and splints the wrist personally. The mission log calls it "nominal". Everyone aboard knows it was more than that.
  kitfrom B A
  move B A
  bond A B 12
  morale B 4
